Rule 1 (input tensors to QFunctional add must have the same dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (QFunctional add_scalar: scalar value must be representable by the tensor's dtype, and tensor must be quantized)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then v_2 ≥ -128 ∧ v_2 ≤ 127 else if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ 255 else if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≥ -32768 ∧ v_2 ≤ 32767 else if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then v_2 ≥ -2147483648 ∧ v_2 ≤ 2147483647
>>
Rule 3 (QFunctional cat operation: tensors must have the same shape except for the concatenation dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_3 < 0 then v_3 ≥ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_3 < 0 else v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i ≠ v_3 then shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 4 (QFunctional mul operation requires two tensor inputs with compatible shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 5 (QFunctional add_relu operation requires two tensor inputs and their shapes are broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1))
>>
Rule 6 (QFunctional add_relu operation: scale and zero_point must be specified if the first tensor is not quantized)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : float, v_4 : int} |= if dtype_(v_1) > 5 then v_3 > 0 ∧ v_4 ≥ -128 ∧ v_4 ≤ 127
